{"url": "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=structural+conditions+for+operationalizing+AI+agency+and+decision+consequence+accountability&format=json&resultType=core&pageSize=4", "scope": "Europe PMC search metadata, abstracts and full-text links; discovery only", "excerpt": "[{"title": "Teaching Craft Intelligence: Sovereignty Protocols for AI-Mediated Student Leadership.", "abstract": "Artificial intelligence (AI) now mediates how student leaders learn and decide, creating a speed imperative that often rewards algorithmic fluency over human judgment and intercultural accountability. This article argues student leadership programs can turn AI from a plagiarism risk into a laboratory for craft intelligence (transforming knowledge and lived experience into sound judgment in action) and deliberate stewardship, which safeguards how knowledge is created, tested, and shared. It maps four perils (e.g., inquiry collapse, context erasure, algorithmic authority, and cultural narrowing) that introduces a Trace of Agency toolkit of four sovereignty protocols to make AI-assisted decisions transparent and leadership claims auditable.", "doi": "10.1002/yd.70070", "pmid": "42753193", "pmcid": "PMC13603953", "source": "MED", "fullTextUrlList": {"fullTextUrl": [{"availability": "Subscription required", "availabilityCode": "S", "documentStyle": "doi", "site": "DOI", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1002/yd.70070"}, {"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentStyle": "html", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13603953"}, {"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentStyle": "pdf", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13603953?pdf=render"}]}}, {"title": "Synthetic gatekeeping in health chatbots: configured answer systems as the unit of AI evaluation and governance for medical information.", "abstract": "Two health chatbots can give the same clinically appropriate advice and still constitute different interventions: one stops at a clinician referral, the other places an affiliated booking one click away. In this Hypothesis and Theory article we argue that the appropriate unit of health-AI evaluation is therefore not the model output alone, but the configured answer system - the large language model (LLM) together with source selection, retrieval, interface, action routing and downstream data return. We call this organizationally configured mode of mediation synthetic gatekeeping. Its necessary core comprises source selection and generative synthesis, with personalization and action routing as extending dimensions; its observable manifestations are content and pathway traces, and its proposed mechanism is infrastructural steering. Content parity does not gu

